<section n="1" image-layout="left" id="q86e187i7b30rse">
<img query="futuristic office with soft blue light, workers and holographic AI interfaces, wide cinematic atmosphere" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;futuristic office with soft blue light, workers and holographic AI interfaces, wide cinematic atmosphere&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;so0GP&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>AI &amp; the Labor Market: Is AI Disrupting the Future of Work?</h1>
<p>A clear-eyed look at what the evidence actually says — and what it means for workers, organizations, and policy.</p></div></section>

<section n="2" image-layout="blank" id="i3dz02s0ldljp2c">







<div class="body">
<h1>The Debate Is Real — and the Stakes Are Enormous</h1>
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/VMSOvYY9Zfap-mZNFpbQI.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><smart-layout variant="stats">
<smart-layout-item number="$31T">
<h4>U.S. Economy</h4>
<p>Nearly 60% is labor costs — even a small AI-driven shift moves trillions.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="300M">
<h4>Jobs at Risk Globally</h4>
<p>~27% of OECD positions could be transformed through AI automation.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="71%">
<h4>Americans Concerned</h4>
<p>Worried AI will put too many people out of work permanently — but the reality is more nuanced.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="3" image-layout="blank" id="odk1f4w13gdqbkr">



<div class="body">
<h1>A Job Is a Bundle of Tasks — Not a Single Thing</h1>
<p>AI almost never wipes out whole jobs overnight. It affects <b>tasks first</b> — some get automated, some get supercharged, and some create entirely new work.</p>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/MfIJj4MZa3u3zYdmzsCic.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<blockquote>"A doctor diagnoses, orders tests, interprets results, and coordinates care. A lawyer drafts, researches, argues, and advises. Each task has a different AI exposure profile."</blockquote>
<p>The task-level lens is essential: it reveals where AI is genuinely disruptive versus where human judgment remains irreplaceable.</p>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="4" image-layout="right" id="7jlg302uqhrd0i0">
<img query="three stacked transparent layers of glass panels glowing in blue and purple light, abstract technology concept" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;three stacked transparent layers of glass panels glowing in blue and purple light, abstract technology concept&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;IRyLj&quot;}" class="accent-image">



<div class="body">
<h1>A Three-Layer Framework for Understanding AI's Impact</h1>
<smart-layout variant="arrows" orientation="vertical" twoSided="false">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 1 — Exposure</h4>
<p>Which tasks can AI plausibly assist or perform today?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 2 — Adoption</h4>
<p>How quickly will organizations actually deploy AI in practice?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Layer 3 — Labor Market Response</h4>
<p>What is the net effect on employment, wages, and new job creation?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout>
<p>These layers constantly feed back into each other — which is precisely why the debate remains so contentious.</p></div></section>

<section n="5" image-layout="blank" id="ko2sc21p3uchn27">







<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 1: Who Is Most Exposed?</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/YUa98dwaWODFnA99ey7mK.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
<aside variant="warning"><b>Highest Exposure</b> — Text-heavy, information-processing roles: legal research, financial analysis, programming, writing, customer support. High-paying, highly educated jobs score highest because their work is language and symbol dense.</aside>
<aside variant="success"><b>Lowest Exposure</b> — Embodied, on-site, and interpersonal roles: electricians, roofers, nursing assistants, athletes. Physical manipulation and rich social interaction remain largely AI-resistant today.</aside>
<p>Unlike earlier automation waves that targeted routine physical tasks, generative AI reaches <b>cognitive, non-routine work</b> once assumed to be safe.</p></div></section>

<section n="6" image-layout="blank" id="gcevhwq56q8ozzp">



<div class="body">
<h1>AI Capabilities Are Racing Ahead of Expectations</h1>
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/0EOfYbjRCdmBrLzAIiyt-.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><smart-layout variant="solidBoxes">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>2024 Milestone</h4>
<p>AI surpassed human baselines in reading comprehension, visual reasoning, PhD-level science, and multimodal understanding.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>The "New Moore's Law"</h4>
<p>AI's autonomous task capacity doubles every ~7 months. By 2027: a full workday. By 2029: a full work month.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="7" image-layout="blank" id="tudrx10be2dbdkt">


<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 2: Exposure ≠ Adoption</h1>
<columns colWidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<h4>What slows deployment?</h4>
<ul>
<li>Legal constraints and regulatory uncertainty</li>
<li>Union rules and collective agreements</li>
<li>Data confidentiality requirements</li>
<li>Customer backlash and trust deficits</li>
<li>Workflow inertia and missing complementary investments</li>
</ul>
<p>A job can be highly exposed in theory but completely untouched in practice.</p>
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/36dqHYHpPqMq2xGj1uh38.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
<p align="center">Generative AI hit <b>54.6%</b> overall adult adoption by August 2025 — up 10 points in a single year. Work-specific adoption reached <b>37.4%</b>, still trailing personal use.</p>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="8" image-layout="blank" id="6lrk1ir60llbdly">



<div class="body">
<h1>The Productivity J-Curve: Why Gains Take Time</h1>
<columns colwidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalalign="center"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/q-WW-hRgYtpndVD52_C_A.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom" align="center"></div>
<div verticalalign="center"><columns colwidths="[50,50]">
<div>
<h4>Historical Pattern</h4>
<p>Electricity took decades to raise factory output. PC productivity gains only appeared in U.S. statistics in the mid-1990s — <b>15 years after launch</b>. AI is following the same arc.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h4>The "Workslop" Problem</h4>
<p>Early AI adoption often dips productivity first. A 2025 Harvard Business Review study found <b>40% of knowledge workers</b> spend ~2 hours/week fixing low-quality AI outputs — before workflows mature and gains accelerate.</p>
</div>
</columns></div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="9" image-layout="right" id="jjn2kc9csx7mvg7">
<img query="radiologist reviewing medical scans on a bright screen in a modern hospital, calm and professional environment" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;radiologist reviewing medical scans on a bright screen in a modern hospital, calm and professional environment&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;Kfdtn&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 1: Augmentation — AI Makes Workers More Productive</h1>
<smart-layout variant="outlineBoxesWithSideLine" orientation="vertical" twoSided="false">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Daily AI Users Win</h4>
<p>Slack's Workforce Index shows daily AI users consistently outperform non-users on productivity, focus, stress management, and job satisfaction. <b>41%</b> rate their productivity "Very Good" vs. <b>26%</b> of non-users.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>The Radiology Lesson</h4>
<p>Geoff Hinton predicted radiologists would be replaced within 5 years (2016). He was right that AI outperforms on benchmarks — but wrong about demand. Radiology continues to grow, a pattern seen across many exposed professions.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="10" image-layout="blank" id="ua61cjcy68q6jko">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 2: Displacement — Real, But Concentrated</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/bbGVZndFwjHmGLZpma0Bu.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<h4>Highest-Risk Roles</h4>
<p>Clerical and back-office work faces the greatest displacement pressure: routine document processing, booking, transcription, and standardized communications are repeatedly flagged as highly automatable.</p>
<blockquote>Andrej Karpathy's rule of thumb: look for jobs that are <i>"repetitive, independent, closed, short, forgiving, and digital"</i> — those are most at risk on shorter timescales.</blockquote>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="11" image-layout="blank" id="su0dnjjy292wiwt">



<div class="body">
<h1>Response 3: Reinstatement — AI Creates New Roles Too</h1>
<p>History shows that technological revolutions rarely destroy jobs in aggregate — they transform them. The PC era created software engineers, IT support, and digital marketers that simply didn't exist before.</p>
<smart-layout variant="iconsText" imagePosition="top">
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="robot arm" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;robot arm&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;H2ouB&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>New AI-Native Roles</h4>
<p>AI engineers, prompt specialists, AI trainers, and trust &amp; safety professionals are already emerging as distinct occupations.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="expanding graph" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;expanding graph&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;P1jqA&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>Expanded Existing Roles</h4>
<p>Productivity gains lower costs and raise demand, broadening scope for workers in many existing occupations.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<icon class="accessory-image" query="balance scale" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;icon&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;balance scale&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;license&quot;:&quot;All&quot;}},&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;4BlKx&quot;}"></icon>
<h4>The Real Challenge</h4>
<p>Pace and distribution of change — who adapts fastest and who benefits most — will define the outcome.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="12" image-layout="blank" id="3mji6dpmtb4nno1">



<div class="body">
<h1>What to Watch: Three Questions That Will Determine the Outcome</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/9yfLWL3zkz5f1WStGFzWZ.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom">
<smart-layout variant="bigBullets" numbered="true">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Will adoption accelerate or plateau?</h4>
<p>If AI capability doubles every 4–7 months, the window for workers and institutions to adapt narrows dramatically.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Who captures the productivity gains?</h4>
<p>Higher-wage, higher-educated workers are most exposed — and most positioned to benefit. Lower-wage workers face less disruption but fewer gains.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>How will policy respond?</h4>
<p>Retraining programs, labor protections, and social safety nets will shape whether AI's abundance is broadly shared or concentrated at the top.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="13" image-layout="blank" id="q7a9j304kpq1hrg">


